configure_tool	CommandSpec { name: "configure_tool", pack_source_sandbox_helper: false, traits: Traits(0), surface: Some([SpecSurface { provider: Core(Tcl), windows: [("8.4", Some("9.2"))] }]), arity: Arity { count: Arguments, min: 0, max: 65535, step: 0, also_exact: None }, arity_windows: [], arg_roles: [], arg_role_resolver: None, arg_role_count_resolver: None, arg_role_layout_resolver: None, arg_role_resolver_roles: [], clause_grammar: None, arg_presentation: [], repeated_args: [], frame_effect: None, clause_shape_check: None, command_prefixes: [], command_prefix_resolver: None, script_timing_resolver: None, script_lookup_scope: None, substitution_resolver: None, callback_taint_inputs: [], return_type: None, return_type_hook: None, var_write_typing: ReturnValue, variable_write_min_args: None, return_elements: None, var_elements_effect: None, representation_effect: None, arg_types: [], subcommands: [], prefix_matching: Enabled, allow_unknown_subcommands: false, default_form_first_word: None, hover: Some(HoverSnippet { summary: "Set the parameters for a tool that Libero SoC runs.", synopsis: ["configure_tool -name tool_name -params parameter:value..."], snippet: "General-purpose command that stores the run-time settings for one Libero tool ahead of run_tool. It takes the tool name and one or more parameter:value pairs, which are split apart and passed to the tool; repeating -params accumulates settings, and repeated configure_tool calls for the same tool are equivalent to one call carrying every pair. Tool parameter vocabularies: COMPILE accepts BLOCK_MODE, ENABLE_DESIGN_SEPARATION, DISPLAY_FANOUT_LIMIT, MERGE_SDC, PDC_IMPORT_HARDERROR, BLOCK_PLACEMENT_CONFLICTS, BLOCK_ROUTING_CONFLICTS, PA4_GB_MAX_RCLKINT_INSERTION, PA4_GB_MIN_GB_FANOUT_TO_USE_RCLKINT, PA4_GB_MAX_FANOUT_DATA_MOVE, PA4_GB_COUNT and SET_MITIGATION on SmartFusion2, IGLOO2 and RTG4, and MERGEPDC and MERGESDC on SmartFusion, IGLOO, ProASIC3 and Fusion. SYNTHESIZE accepts CLOCK_ASYNC, CLOCK_GLOBAL, CLOCK_DATA, RAM_OPTIMIZED_FOR_POWER, RETIMING, SYNPLIFY_OPTIONS, SYNPLIFY_TCL_FILE, BLOCK_MODE, BLOCK_PLACEMENT_CONFLICTS, BLOCK_ROUTING_CONFLICTS, PA4_GB_COUNT, PA4_GB_MAX_RCLKINT_INSERTION, PA4_GB_MIN_GB_FANOUT_TO_USE_RCLKINT, LANGUAGE_SYSTEM_VLOG, LANGUAGE_VERILOG_2001 and LANGUAGE_VHDL_2008. PLACEROUTE accepts TDPR, PDPR, EFFORT_LEVEL, INCRPLACEANDROUTE, REPAIR_MIN_DELAY, NUM_MULTI_PASSES, START_SEED_INDEX, MULTI_PASS_LAYOUT, MULTI_PASS_CRITERIA, SPECIFIC_CLOCK, DELAY_ANALYSIS, STOP_ON_FIRST_PASS, SLACK_CRITERIA, RGB_COUNT and REPLICATION on SmartFusion2, IGLOO2 and RTG4, and TDPR and INCRPLACEANDROUTE on the older families. FLASH_FREEZE accepts FF_RAM_STATE and FF_MSS_CLOCK. PROGRAMDEVICE accepts prog_action and prog_optional_procedures. PROGRAM_OPTIONS accepts program_envm, program_fabric, program_mode and program_security. PROGRAM_RECOVERY accepts enable_auto_update, enable_prog_recovery, spi_clk_freq and spi_data_transfer_mode. PROGRAMMING_BITSTREAM_SETTINGS, for RTG4, accepts system_controller_suspend_mode, disable_digest_check, disable_jtag, disable_fabric_erase_write_verify, disable_probe_read_write, disable_spi and one_time_programmable. PROGRAMMER_INFO accepts the per-programmer settings flashpro3_clk_mode, flashpro3_force_freq, flashpro3_freq and flashpro3_vpump and their flashpro4_ and flashpro5_ equivalents, plus flashpro_drive_trst, flashpro_force_freq, flashpro_force_vddp, flashpro_freq, flashpro_vddl, flashpro_vddp, flashpro_vpn, flashpro_vpp and the flashprolite_ set. SPM accepts the security policy settings back_level_bypass, back_level_protection, back_level_update_version, debug_cortex_m3, debug_digest_request, debug_disable_jtag, debug_passkey, debug_ujtag_access, factory_access, iap_isp_services, security_key_mode, smartdebug_access, the update_ and use_ policy locks, and the user_encryption_key and user_passkey values. USER_PROG_DATA accepts design_version and silicon_signature. EXPORTPIN accepts PINRPT_BY_NAME and PINRPT_BY_NUMBER. PUBLISHBLOCK accepts LANGUAGE, PLACEMENT, ROUTING and REGION. CONFIGURE_PROG_OPTIONS, CONFIGURE_PROG_OPTIONS_RTG4, IO_PROGRAM_STATE, INIT_LOCK, GENERATEPROGRAMMINGDATA, GENERATEPROGRAMMINGFILE and VERIFYTIMING are configured through the separate SmartFusion2, IGLOO2 and RTG4 Tcl for SoC document or take no configure parameters.", source: "Libero SoC v11.8 Tcl Command Reference", examples: "configure_tool -name {COMPILE}  -params {DISPLAY_FANOUT_LIMIT:10}  -params {MERGE_SDC:true}\nconfigure_tool -name {SYNTHESIZE} -params {LANGUAGE_VHDL_2008:true}", return_value: "0 on success and 1 on failure." }), forms: [FormSpec { kind: Default, synopsis: "configure_tool -name tool_name -params parameter:value...", surface: None, lifecycle: Lifecycle { introduced: None, deprecated: None, retired: None, deprecation_fix: None } }], command_forms: [], semantic_operation: None, semantic_operation_windows: [], completion: None, result_stability: None, native_result: None, assigns_variable_at: None, safe_on_uninit: None, const_fold: None, const_fold_versioned: None, lowering_hook: None, bpf_op: None, codegen_hook: None, codegen_hook_windows: [], inline_codegen_hook: None, inline_codegen_hook_windows: [], native_lowering: None, native_lowering_windows: [], semantics: Inherited, analyser_hook: None, command_table_effect: None, side_effects: [], world_effects: None, state_transitions: None, dispatch_dependencies: None, literal_argument_validator: None, source_index_bounds: None, inferred_storage_type: None, required_package: Some("libero"), tk_geometry: None, excluded_events: [], unsafe_command: false, closed_value_args: [], arg_values_accept_prefix: false, event_requires: None, event_requirement_forms: [], event_emits: None, event_emission_forms: [], data_collection: None, irules_source_flow: None, side_switch_target: None, event_handler_priority: None, irules_top_level_effect: None, options: [OptionSpec { name: "-name", value: Takes(OptionArg { arity: One, role: Value, also_role: None, taints_var