is_design_state_complete	CommandSpec { name: "is_design_state_complete", pack_source_sandbox_helper: false, traits: Traits(0), surface: Some([SpecSurface { provider: Core(Tcl), windows: [("8.4", Some("9.2"))] }]), arity: Arity { count: Arguments, min: 1, max: 1, step: 0, also_exact: None }, arity_windows: [], arg_roles: [], arg_role_resolver: None, arg_role_count_resolver: None, arg_role_layout_resolver: None, arg_role_resolver_roles: [], clause_grammar: None, arg_presentation: [], repeated_args: [], frame_effect: None, clause_shape_check: None, command_prefixes: [], command_prefix_resolver: None, script_timing_resolver: None, script_lookup_scope: None, substitution_resolver: None, callback_taint_inputs: [], return_type: None, return_type_hook: None, var_write_typing: ReturnValue, variable_write_min_args: None, return_elements: None, var_elements_effect: None, representation_effect: None, arg_types: [], subcommands: [], prefix_matching: Enabled, allow_unknown_subcommands: false, default_form_first_word: None, hover: Some(HoverSnippet { summary: "Report whether a given design state is valid.", synopsis: ["is_design_state_complete value"], snippet: "Returns a Boolean value telling whether the named design state is valid, where value is one of SETUP_DESIGN for a loaded design whose family is set, DEVICE_SELECTION for a completed set_device, NETLIST_IMPORT for an imported netlist, COMPILE, LAYOUT, BACKANNOTATE for an exported post-layout timing file, or PROGRAMMING_FILES for an exported programming file. Because certain commands can be used only after compile or layout, a script checks the design state with this command before calling them. It returns an error if no design is loaded, if more than one argument is passed, or if the argument is not one of the valid values.", source: "Libero SoC v11.8 Tcl Command Reference", examples: "set bLayoutDone [ is_design_state_complete LAYOUT ]", return_value: "1 when the named design state is valid; otherwise 0." }), forms: [FormS