report	CommandSpec { name: "report", pack_source_sandbox_helper: false, traits: Traits(0), surface: Some([SpecSurface { provider: Core(Tcl), windows: [("8.4", Some("9.2"))] }]), arity: Arity { count: Arguments, min: 1, max: 65535, step: 0, also_exact: None }, arity_windows: [], arg_roles: [], arg_role_resolver: None, arg_role_count_resolver: None, arg_role_layout_resolver: None, arg_role_resolver_roles: [], clause_grammar: None, arg_presentation: [], repeated_args: [], frame_effect: None, clause_shape_check: None, command_prefixes: [], command_prefix_resolver: None, script_timing_resolver: None, script_lookup_scope: None, substitution_resolver: None, callback_taint_inputs: [], return_type: None, return_type_hook: None, var_write_typing: ReturnValue, variable_write_min_args: None, return_elements: None, var_elements_effect: None, representation_effect: None, arg_types: [], subcommands: [], prefix_matching: Enabled, allow_unknown_subcommands: false, default_form_first_word: None, hover: Some(HoverSnippet { summary: "Generate a report of the chosen type into the named file.", synopsis: ["report -type type ?-analysis value? ?-format value? ?options? filename"], snippet: "One command generates every Libero SoC report kind, selected by -type and written to the trailing filename. The timing and timing violations reports take -analysis, -print_summary, -print_paths, -use_slack_threshold with -slack_threshold, -max_paths, -max_expanded_paths, -limit_max_paths, -include_user_sets, -include_pin_to_pin, -include_clock_domains, -select_clock_domains, and -clock_domain; datasheet takes only -format; bottleneck takes -cost_type, -max_instances, -max_paths, -max_parallel_paths, -analysis, and the pruning options -set_name, -clock with -set_type, -from_clock with -to_clock, -source_clock with -sink_clock, -from, -to, -source, -sink, and -in_to_out; constraints_coverage and combinational_loops take no options of their own. The power report takes -powerunit, -frequnit, -opcond, -opmode, -toggle, the summary switches such as -power_summary, -rail_breakdown, -type_breakdown, -clock_breakdown, -thermal_summary, -battery_life, -opcond_summary, -clock_summary, -instance_breakdown, -activity_summary, -enablerates_summary, and -with_annotation_coverage, plus the filters -power_threshold with -min_power, -filter_instance with -max_instance, -frequency_threshold with -min_frequency, -filter_pin with -max_pin, and the -style, -sortby, and -sortorder presentation options; power_history takes only a .txt filename; and power_activity_map reads a VCD file named by -vcd_file with -partial_parse, -start_time, -end_time, -auto_detect_top_level_name, -top_level_name, -report_type, -report_query, -max_net, -max_cycle, -clock_settings, -glitch_filtering, -glitch_threshold, -auto_construct_clock_domain, -clock_period, and -clock_offset. The timing and timing violations reports are SmartTime-specific and run in batch mode only through run_tool -name {VERIFYTIMING} -script; the guide also names status, pin, flip-flop, I/O bank, and global usage reports without giving their -type spelling, and records -annotated_pins, -stat_pow, and -dyn_pow as removed arguments that now only raise a warning.", source: "Libero SoC v11.8 Tcl Command Reference", examples: "report -type timing -print_summary no -analysis max  -use_slack_threshold yes -slack_threshold 0.50  -print_paths yes -max_paths 3 -max_expanded_paths 0  timing_report.txt\nreport -type bottleneck -cost_type path_count -slack_threshold 0 -set_name set1  -max_paths 10 -max_parallel_paths 10 -analysis max -format text bottleneck.txt\nreport -type datasheet -format Text datasheet.txt", return_value: "Not documented in the command reference." }), forms: [FormSpec { kind: Default, synopsis: "report -type type ?-analysis value? ?-format value? ?options? filename", surface: None, lifecycle: Lifecycle { introduced: None, deprecated: None, retired: None, deprecation_fix: None } }], command_forms: [], semantic_operation: None, s