run_tool	CommandSpec { name: "run_tool", pack_source_sandbox_helper: false, traits: Traits(0), surface: Some([SpecSurface { provider: Core(Tcl), windows: [("8.4", Some("9.2"))] }]), arity: Arity { count: Arguments, min: 0, max: 65535, step: 0, also_exact: None }, arity_windows: [], arg_roles: [], arg_role_resolver: None, arg_role_count_resolver: None, arg_role_layout_resolver: None, arg_role_resolver_roles: [], clause_grammar: None, arg_presentation: [], repeated_args: [], frame_effect: None, clause_shape_check: None, command_prefixes: [], command_prefix_resolver: None, script_timing_resolver: None, script_lookup_scope: None, substitution_resolver: None, callback_taint_inputs: [], return_type: None, return_type_hook: None, var_write_typing: ReturnValue, variable_write_min_args: None, return_elements: None, var_elements_effect: None, representation_effect: None, arg_types: [], subcommands: [], prefix_matching: Enabled, allow_unknown_subcommands: false, default_form_first_word: None, hover: Some(HoverSnippet { summary: "Start the specified Libero SoC tool.", synopsis: ["run_tool -name tool_name ?-script script_file?"], snippet: "Runs one Libero tool with whatever settings configure_tool stored for it; for tools that support command files an optional command file is supplied through -script. Where possible the tool_name matches the name of the tool in Libero SoC, and invoking a tool automatically runs the upstream tools it depends on, so running COMPILE runs synthesis first. Tool names: SYNTHESIZE runs synthesis on the design and accepts -script. COMPILE runs Compile with default or configured settings. SIM_PRESYNTH, SIM_POSTSYNTH and SIM_POSTLAYOUT run pre-synthesis, post-synthesis and post-layout simulation with the default simulation tool. PLACEROUTE runs Layout with default or configured settings. VERIFYTIMING runs timing analysis, with SmartTime-specific commands supplied through -script on SmartFusion2, IGLOO2 and RTG4. VERIFYPOWER runs power analysis, with SmartPower-specific commands supplied through -script. GENERATEPROGRAMMINGFILE generates the bitstream used for programming within Libero, and GENERATEPROGRAMMINGDATA generates the files needed to produce programming bitstream files. GENERATE_MEMORY_MAP exports an XML data sheet describing the root SmartDesign of the project. PROGRAMDEVICE programs the device with the configured parameters. CONFIGURE_CHAIN takes a -script of FlashPro-specific commands and passes them to FlashPro Express to configure the JTAG chain, generating the project-management commands itself. SMARTDEBUG takes a -script of SmartDebug-specific commands. SSNANALYZER takes a -script of Simultaneous Switching Noise commands and generates a noise margin report for I/Os after layout. UPDATE_ENVM, on SmartFusion2 and IGLOO2, and UPDATE_UPROM, on RTG4, take a -script update configuration file that updates the ENVM or UPROM storage clients. EXPORTPIN exports the pin report file after configure_tool -name EXPORTPIN, EXPORTSDF exports the backannotated SDF delay file and Verilog or VHDL netlist, EXPORTIBIS exports the I/O Buffer Information Specification file, and EXPORTPROGRAMMINGFILE runs FlashPro in batch mode to export a STAPL file with all features available in the design. PUBLISHBLOCK publishes block information for the bottom-up block design flow, and SOFTWAREIDE runs SoftConsole, IAR or Keil, whichever is selected in the tool profile.", source: "Libero SoC v11.8 Tcl Command Reference", examples: "run_tool -name {COMPILE}\nrun_tool  -name {SYNTHESIZE} -script {./control_synopsys.tcl}\nrun_tool  -name {VERIFYPOWER}  -script {./SmartPower.tcl}", return_value: "0 on success and 1 on failure." }), forms: [FormSpec { kind: Default, synopsis: "run_tool -name tool_name ?-script script_file?", surface: None, lifecycle: Lifecycle { introduced: None, deprecated: None, retired: None, deprecation_fix: None } }], command_forms: [], semantic_operation: None, semantic_operation_windows: [], completion: None, result_st